From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:03:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/hevc: set slices aside only where setup ends at a
 second layer

ffmpeg-9974 sets the slice data of a picture aside when setup ends at a
later NAL unit than the base picture's first slice. That is meant for a
picture of two layers, whose setup ends at the second layer's first
slice; but a single-layer stream with a VPS, SPS or PPS after the first
slice of a picture ends its setup there too, and took the same path.
Set slices aside only where the NAL unit at which setup ends belongs to
a layer above the base: a single-layer stream decodes as it does without
ffmpeg-9974, and a picture of two layers as with it.

find_finish_setup_nal() returns the index of a NAL unit of the packet,
so the NAL unit read is in it (the comparison before it holds only then
too).

The condition is cinemaONE's: he gave it in Hades issue 34 as the one
of his port of ffmpeg-9974 to FFmpeg master (pull request 26397 on
code.ffmpeg.org), taking up a case noticed in the review of ffmpeg-9974.
---
 libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
index b45777f..f705519 100644
--- a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
@@ -3685,11 +3685,14 @@ static int hevc_frame_start(HEVCContext *s, HEVCLayerContext *l,
         s->finish_setup_nal_idx = find_finish_setup_nal(s);
         // setup ends at a later layer's first slice: hold back the slice data
         // until then, so the next frame thread does not wait for this picture
-        // (nothing to hold back where its samples come from the separate decoder)
+        // (nothing to hold back where its samples come from the separate decoder,
+        // nor where setup ends at a NAL unit of the base layer: a single-layer
+        // stream with a parameter set after its first slice decodes as before)
         s->defer_slices = s->avctx->active_thread_type == FF_THREAD_FRAME &&
                           !s->avctx->hwaccel &&
                           s->base_mode != HEVC_BASE_LAYER_USED &&
-                          s->finish_setup_nal_idx > nal_idx;
+                          s->finish_setup_nal_idx > nal_idx &&
+                          s->pkt.nals[s->finish_setup_nal_idx].nuh_layer_id > 0;
 
         // with a separate decoder of the base layer: the picture is all intra
         // as far as its slice headers read before setup ends say (decode_slice()),
